// Pushing the expectation into the arms makes the ARM the reporting site: a genuinely ill-typed arm
// is E0007 at the arm's own body, not at the whole `match`. It is reported exactly once — the joined
// result is deliberately not re-subsumed at the `match`, which would duplicate the same mismatch on
// a span covering every (correct) arm too.
// expect: error E0007 at 10:14
// expect: exit 1
fn describe(x: int): Map<string, int> {
    return match x {
        1 => {"a": 1},
        _ => 5,
    }
}

echo describe(1).len();
